	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"Walk the whole village before changing it. Locate beds, job blocks, food, wells, entrances and nearby hazards; then mark the settlement on the shared map."
				"Villagers need safe paths between workstations and beds. Decorative clutter, trapdoors and complicated stairs can look excellent while making daily routines fail."
				"In the field-guide lore, a village survives because many small routines overlap. Repair those routines before replacing the buildings that express them."
				"Guard Villagers need clear routes, lighting, equipment, and a raid plan. Decorative walls are not protection if gates remain open, roofs spawn enemies, or villagers cannot retreat from the bell to safe beds."
			]
			id: "024141EA5AB0B169"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6A38A8B60A3DD629"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "A settlement is a system, not a box of free beds"
			tasks: [{
				id: "121140413D5D5690"
				title: "I read this lesson and tried it in the world"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Read the Village Before Rebuilding"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["024141EA5AB0B169"]
			description: [
				"Light streets and roofs, close dangerous drops, and build a readable perimeter. Guard Villagers can help defend a town, but walls and sight lines still matter."
				"Avoid cramming every villager into a permanent trading cell. A compact trade hall can be useful, but the pack is at its best when settlements remain believable and navigable."
				"Keep raids away from unfinished villages. Bad Omen is a group decision when other players' villagers are at risk."
				"Guard Villagers need clear routes, lighting, equipment, and a raid plan. Decorative walls are not protection if gates remain open, roofs spawn enemies, or villagers cannot retreat from the bell to safe beds."
			]
			id: "54F5458D64A67BBB"
			rewards: [{
				id: "13FDEF1C7A9CC18E"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Safety should still look like a place people live"
			tasks: [{
				id: "27A0AF20EB647B2C"
				title: "I read this lesson and tried it in the world"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Secure, Do Not Imprison"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["024141EA5AB0B169"]
			description: [
				"A villager claims a nearby workstation to gain a profession. Trade during working hours, leave the workstation reachable, and confirm that valuable villagers can restock."
				"Prices react to demand, reputation and curing. Buy what the settlement can sustainably produce instead of repeatedly exhausting one trade."
				"Label specialist buildings so everyone knows where librarians, farmers, smiths and cartographers belong."
				"Villagers restock only when they can reach and use the correct job site under valid conditions. If a trade locks up, inspect pathfinding, workstation ownership, time of day, and safety before adding more villagers."
			]
			id: "44DA62AABA3492AB"
			rewards: [{
				id: "0C326E512DDE8A0C"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "A workstation is both profession and schedule"
			tasks: [{
				id: "43B6DB5A75EB1D7E"
				title: "I read this lesson and tried it in the world"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Jobs, Trades and Restocks"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["54F5458D64A67BBB", "44DA62AABA3492AB"]
			description: [
				"Bountiful boards offer requests with listed rewards. Read both sides carefully, check JEI for the requested item, and avoid spending unique progression materials on a weak payout."
				"Choose bounties that fit work the group already wants to do: harvest surplus, clear known threats or deliver materials from an upcoming expedition."
				"A good bounty creates direction without becoming compulsory homework. Let expired or unreasonable offers go."
				"Bountiful boards generate jobs that request items and offer rewards. Read the entire bounty, reserve shared essentials, and accept work that fits current plans rather than draining the pantry for a shiny but unhelpful prize."
			]
			id: "1BF2742EDAD74DF2"
			rewards: [{
				id: "26E3AF0FFE503E14"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 15
			}]
			subtitle: "Turn ordinary work into a shared expedition fund"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4981C267C5DF447C"
				title: "I read this lesson and tried it in the world"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "The Bounty Board"
			x: 4.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["44DA62AABA3492AB"]
			description: [
				"Build several honest sources of emeralds rather than one exploitative loop. Farmers, fletchers, masons and shepherds can reward different parts of a healthy homestead."
				"Keep a public emergency reserve for maps, name tags, rare books and group projects. Personal wealth is useful; shared liquidity saves expeditions."
				"Never reroll a friend's named or levelled villager without asking. Their trade history is part of the settlement."
				"A living settlement has public food, readable storage, professions, transport, defence, and room to grow. The Steward's Charter judges success by whether residents and new players can use the town without constant rescue."
			]
			id: "35046621C94B6A6D"
