		{
			dependencies: ["1BF2742EDAD74DF2", "35046621C94B6A6D"]
			description: [
				"Group related professions around a visible purpose: farmers near produce stalls, smiths by the forge, librarians around records and maps."
				"Use signs, item frames and colour sparingly so visitors can identify trades without inspecting every villager. Leave enough room for multiplayer crowds."
				"Markets are where homesteading, exploration and building meet. The best one tells newcomers what the settlement can make."
				"A living settlement has public food, readable storage, professions, transport, defence, and room to grow. The Steward's Charter judges success by whether residents and new players can use the town without constant rescue."
			]
			id: "5EF9AC708BE10640"
