			description: [
				"Confirm that villagers sleep, restock and survive the night; that guards can move; and that visitors can find food, trades and exits."
				"Choose one public improvement based on a real problem: clinic, market, wall, rail stop, farm, inn or archive. Finish it before beginning three replacements."
				"A steward does not own the village. They make it easier for the next person to care for it."
				"A living settlement has public food, readable storage, professions, transport, defence, and room to grow. The Steward's Charter judges success by whether residents and new players can use the town without constant rescue."
