		{
			dependencies: ["0BA84AFD5BCEC392"]
			description: [
				"Bountiful boards appear in villages and generate bounties that request items in exchange for rewards. Read every objective, reward, quantity, and time condition before accepting or taking a bounty."
				"Choose work that overlaps farming, fishing, building, or exploration already planned. Do not empty public food, rare breeding stock, museum pieces, or machine reserves merely because a board assigned them a value."
				"Maintain an accepted-work chest, a completed-contract record, and a clear rule for communal ingredients. The board becomes interesting when it creates stories and circulation, not when one player silently strips every profitable offer."
			]
			id: "22CC2FF8449941A3"
